WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Electricity runs everything in an HVAC system. If you don't understand it, you
can't diagnose anything.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Wiring diagrams are the roadmaps of HVAC systems. There are two types: schematic
diagrams (show the electrical logic — which components connect to which) and
pictorial diagrams (show the physical location of components and wire routing).

00:00:40.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Schematic Diagram: Shows electrical connections logically — which components are
in series or parallel. Used for troubleshooting circuit logic.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Pictorial Diagram: Shows physical wire routing and component locations. Used for
finding components and tracing wires on the actual equipment.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Series Circuit: Components connected end-to-end. Current flows through each one.
If any component opens, the entire circuit stops. Safety switches are wired in
series.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Here's why this matters on the job: On a no-cooling call, you trace the 24V
circuit: transformer → thermostat → safety switches → contactor coil. If you
find 24V at the thermostat but 0V at the contactor, the problem is between those

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Watch out for these: Always check the wiring diagram on the equipment — do not
assume all systems are wired the same. And — A broken wire in a series circuit
stops everything downstream

00:02:40.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Take a minute before you move on. What's the one thing from this lesson you need
to remember on a service call?

